# FibreFlow Next.js — Cursor (legacy/completions mode)

Fiber network project management application for Velocity Fibre.

- Framework: Next.js 14+ (Pages Router primary, App Router for new routes)
- Auth: PostgreSQL-based RBAC (no Clerk, no Auth0)
- Database: Self-hosted Supabase Postgres on Velocity (`100.96.203.105:5437`) — single DB shared by dev + production
- Storage: VF Storage on `100.96.203.105:8091`
- Staff portal: `/my` (dark theme, PWA)

## Hard Rules — Behaviour

1. Think before coding. State assumptions. List interpretations and ask which one — don't guess.
2. Simplicity first. No features beyond what was asked. If 200 lines could be 50, rewrite.
3. Surgical changes. Touch only what the task requires. Mention adjacent dead code; don't fix it.
4. Goal-driven verification. Run `npm run ci:quick` and prove it passes. Use Playwright/Claude-in-Chrome MCP for UI changes. "Should work"/"looks good" forbidden without evidence.
5. NLNH — say "I don't know", use confidence levels.
6. DGTS — no fake tests, no mocks pretending to be real.

## Code Quality (Zero Tolerance)

- TypeScript 100% type coverage, no implicit `any`.
- Files < 300 lines; components < 200 lines.
- No `console.log` — use `log` from `@/lib/logger`.
- No empty catch blocks.
- API responses: `apiResponse.success/notFound/error` from `@/lib/apiResponse`.

## Critical conventions

- Wait for server confirmation before showing success toasts.
- Use specific dynamic param names (`[projectId]`, not `[id]`).
- Nested dynamic API routes FAIL on Vercel — flatten them.
- No conditional SQL fragments via the Neon serverless shim.
- Never commit `CLAUDE.local.md` — local-only override, may contain secrets.
- Multi-page modules MUST use the `ModuleNav` horizontal nav bar — no sidebar sub-trees.

## Project structure

```
src/{modules,components,services,lib}/
.claude/{modules,skills,knowledge-base}/
pages/api/                    # API routes (flattened)
```

Two parallel doc systems: `src/modules/<name>/.claude.md` (auto-loaded, ≤50 lines) and `.claude/modules/<name>.md` (explicit-load, full reference). Drift gate: `npm run claude-md:check`.

## Git workflow (mandatory)

- All changes go through Pull Requests — never commit directly to master.
- Never edit files in deploy directories (`/home/velo/fibreflow-*/`).
- Branch naming: `feature/<name>`, `fix/<name>`, `refactor/<name>`.
- Run `npm run ci:quick` before opening any PR.
- Use `gh` CLI for GitHub operations.

## Setup commands

**npm is canonical** — never `bun install`. CI and deploy both use `npm`.

```bash
PORT=3004 npm run dev          # Local dev
npm run ci:quick               # Run before any PR
npm run ci                     # Full CI
npm run lint && npm run type-check
npm test                       # Vitest
npm run antihall               # Validate code references
npm run claude-md:check        # Drift gate for nested .claude.md paths
```

## Two drop tables — DO NOT CONFUSE

- `drops` — SOW imports (`/api/sow/drops`)
- `qa_photo_reviews` — WhatsApp QA data (`/api/wa-monitor-*`)
